{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":78894,"duration_api_ms":78071,"num_turns":30,"result":"I rewrote `CLAUDE.md` in place. I didn't run any builds, and I couldn't run any `git` commands because the sandbox blocked them. Everything in it comes from reading the Makefiles, the CI workflows, `.gitmodules`, `src/scripts/` and the READMEs.\n\nThe old file was mostly right but missed several things, which the new one adds:\n\n- **Two toolchains:** Lessons 0–10 use eunomia-bpf (`ecc` and `ecli`) and have no Makefile. Lessons 11 and up use libbpf with a Makefile in each lesson folder. The old file said every tutorial has a Makefile.\n- **Build pipeline:** it now describes the full chain, including the master `src/Makefile` and `V=1` for verbose output.\n- **Testing:** there is no test suite. CI builds each lesson and runs it under `sudo timeout -s 2 3`, treating exit code 124 as success.\n- **Documentation conventions:** each lesson has a Chinese README beside the English one, there is a table-of-contents generator, and the two tutorial style guides in `src/scripts/` are referenced.\n- **Third-party dependencies:** `src/third_party/libbpf` was an empty folder here, and only `blazesym` and `bpftool` are listed in `.gitmodules`. I added a fallback of running `git submodule update --init --recursive` and cloning `libbpf/libbpf` into that folder if it is still empty. I haven't tried that fallback.\n\nI dropped the old directory-by-topic list because it was wrong in places and easy to rediscover from the folder names.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c8f5ef01-cfa1-4a0e-9ef7-d8f41a64755a","total_cost_usd":0.44715809999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29206,"cache_read_input_tokens":634612,"output_tokens":9810,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":29206},"infer